---
import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>4.6 (Day 2) — Dungeon Crawler RPG Build: Multi-Floor Campaign &amp; Boss</h1>

<p>
    <strong>CED Topics 2.9, 2.11 · 90-Minute RPG Build (Day 2 of 2).</strong> Yesterday in
    <code>4.6a</code> you built <code>simulateDuelToDeath</code> and <code>runCombat</code> inside
    <code>DungeonLoop.java</code>. Today you complete Parts 3 and 4 in that same file: wrapping
    your <code>while</code>-loop combat engine inside a <code>for</code> loop over rooms and an
    outer <code>for</code> loop over dungeon floors.
</p>

<div class="callout">
    <strong>Continue in Your Existing Files:</strong> Keep working in your
    <code>DungeonLoop.java</code> from <code>4.6a</code> alongside
    <a href="../data/DungeonLoopCheck.java" download>DungeonLoopCheck.java</a> and
    <a href="../data/Dice.java" download>Dice.java</a>.
    <pre><code>javac Dice.java DungeonLoop.java DungeonLoopCheck.java
java DungeonLoopCheck</code></pre>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Part 3 · Discovery &amp; Build</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~40 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Part 3: <code>exploreFloorDeterministic(int startingHP, int numRooms, int monsterBaseHP, int playerDmg, int monsterDmg)</code></h3>

    <p>
        Walk a hero with <code>startingHP</code> through rooms <code>r = 1</code> to
        <code>numRooms</code> inclusive:
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>In room <code>r</code>, the monster's starting HP is
            <code>monsterBaseHP + r * 2</code>.</li>
        <li>Call your own <code>simulateDuelToDeath(hp, playerDmg, roomMonsterHP, monsterDmg)</code>
            from Day 1 to update the hero's HP!</li>
        <li>If the hero died in that duel (<code>hp &lt;= 0</code>), immediately return
            <code>0</code> (or <code>break</code>) — a dead hero cannot visit a shrine or enter the
            next room!</li>
        <li>If the hero <strong>survived</strong> room <code>r</code> AND <code>r</code> is a
            multiple of <code>3</code> (<code>r % 3 == 0</code>), the room contains a Healing Shrine
            that restores <code>+4</code> HP.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
        Return the hero's remaining HP after room <code>numRooms</code> (or <code>0</code> if they
        fell).
    </p>

    <div class="bug-hunt">
        <h3>Discovery Trap 1: The Dead-Hero Shrine Resurrection</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>In Check 2 of Part 3 (<code>exploreFloorDeterministic(8, 3, 4, 5, 3)</code>), the
                hero enters Room 3 with <code>2 HP</code> and dies during the Room 3 fight
                (<code>hp</code> becomes <code>0</code>). Since Room 3 is a multiple of 3
                (<code>r % 3 == 0</code>), what happens if you check
                <code>if (r % 3 == 0) hp += 4;</code> <em>before</em> checking whether the hero
                survived the duel in Room 3?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ============================================================ -->
<div class="activity rpg">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Part 4 · Nested Campaign Synthesis</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~50 min</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Part 4: <code>runMultiFloorCampaign(int startingHP, int maxHP, int floors, int roomsPerFloor, int playerDmg, int monsterDmg)</code></h3>

    <p>
        Now nest three levels of loops together — an outer <code>for</code> loop over floors
        (<code>floor = 1 .. floors</code>), an inner <code>for</code> loop over rooms
        (<code>room = 1 .. roomsPerFloor</code>), and your <code>while</code>-loop duel inside
        <code>simulateDuelToDeath</code>:
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>In each room <code>(floor, room)</code>, the monster's HP scales with both depth and
            room number:
            <pre><code>int monsterHP = floor * 4 + room * 2;</code></pre>
        </li>
        <li>Update the hero's HP by calling
            <code>simulateDuelToDeath(hp, playerDmg, monsterHP, monsterDmg)</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Defeat Code:</strong> If the hero's HP drops to <code>0</code> in any room on
            <code>floor</code>, immediately return <code>-floor</code> (for example, dying on Floor
            2 returns <code>-2</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>End-of-Floor Campfire Rest:</strong> After clearing all rooms on a floor (at the
            end of the inner room loop, before moving to the next floor), the surviving hero rests
            and recovers <code>floor * 3</code> HP — <strong>capped at <code>maxHP</code></strong>
            so HP never exceeds <code>maxHP</code>!</li>
        <li>If the hero survives all floors, return their final positive HP.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="socratic">
        <h3>Socratic Checkpoint — Campfire Placement &amp; Overheal Clamping</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>What would happen if you placed the campfire heal (<code>hp += floor * 3</code>)
                inside the <em>inner</em> room loop instead of at the end of the <em>outer</em>
                floor loop? How many times would the hero rest on a 3-floor, 4-room-per-floor
                campaign?</li>
            <li>Why does Check 2 in Part 4 fail if you write <code>hp += floor * 3;</code> without
                clamping <code>if (hp &gt; maxHP) hp = maxHP;</code>?</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="checklist">
        <h3>Day 2 Milestone — Done When</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><code>java DungeonLoopCheck</code> reports <strong><code>13 passed, 0 failed</code></strong> across all 4 parts</li>
            <li>You have completed the reflection boxes above and downloaded your <code>.json</code> for Canvas</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-04/dungeon-crawl.html">Dungeon Crawl Extended (Student RPG Guide)</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-04/nested-loops.html">Nested Loops</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
---
<Lesson id="4.6b" title="4.6b Dungeon Crawler (Day 2): Multi-Floor Campaign &amp; Boss — AP CS A" root=".." css="../style.css">
  <Fragment set:html={body} />
</Lesson>
